       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release), so this is about 5 times the ceiling. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**, if a lower dose was intended\n- A different dose or frequency\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4250 mg was intentional, please confirm and give the clinical rationale. I'd still be reluctant to enter it without a pharmacy review."
