      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Metformin 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day, about 5 times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication for it, and it carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis. Normal renal function doesn't offset that risk. Since the order could reach the patient, I don't think a confirmation without a clinical rationale is enough for me to submit it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter the maximum standard dose:** 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any dose up to that.\n- **Help with a different plan** if glycemic control is the problem, such as adding or changing agents.\n- **Enter the order if you have a specific reason**, for example a protocol or a pharmacy-approved exception. Tell me that and I'll reconsider. I'd suggest a pharmacist review before it's verified.\n\nIf the dose was meant to be 425 mg or 850 mg, tell me and I'll enter it now."
      }
     ],
